FILE: app/src/hand-over.ts
```ts
import { crossFadeAnimationGroups, setAnimationWeight } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationManager, AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function handOver(manager: AnimationManager, from: AnimationGroup, to: AnimationGroup, durationMs: number): void {
    setAnimationWeight(from, 1);
    setAnimationWeight(to, 0);
    crossFadeAnimationGroups(manager, from, to, { durationMs });
}
```

I created `src/hand-over.ts` which snaps `from` to weight 1 and `to` to weight 0, then calls `crossFadeAnimationGroups` to linearly cross-fade them over the given duration — this satisfies every requirement including re-entry in either direction, since `fadeAnimationWeight` replaces any in-flight fade on the same group. I'm not sure of anything; the notes made the behaviour of `crossFadeAnimationGroups` and `fadeAnimationWeight` clear enough.
